    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "has really been a scourge in our country, especially in the black communities. The amount of babies that have been aborted, just think about the black population in America could have actually grown substantially over that time. So it's been a very personal topic, very divisive topic in our country. But the one thing you are correct in is that for 50 years, the left has positioned this issue as if it's a right, without balancing it amongst the other rights, like the right of the unborn to live, the right for a lot of other things. When they've done that, frankly, unfortunately, quite successfully, for so long, you have a lot of people who really believe that to be the case. So my view is that it's going to take time for the country to understand the new politics of abortion and what that sweet spot is. And it's really going to take time, I think, for pro-life activists to see the world they want to see, because people now have to live in the new reality of the 50 states making decisions. And so it takes time for the politics of that to center around where the culture is. Ben Shapiro, love and listen to him a lot. He always says, politics is downstream from culture. Abortion is no different. And the tragedy in the United States is abortion has become a part of our culture. The positives are is that there are a lot of young people who are actually pro-life. Like they want to save lives. They want to have their children. They don't want to seek abortion. And so I think that it's going to take us time to move into this new realm of the new politics. I guess you would say of abortion and what that means in the United States. I think where it's really going to end up is California. It's frankly going to be abortion till birth. and same as New York, maybe same as Oregon and Washington State. Mississippi, Alabama, it's going to be no. We're not allowing abortions or six weeks, like which is the law in Florida now, or 10 weeks in some states. And you're really going to have a hybrid approach. What I think is going to happen is America is going to slowly downshift much more to what the standards are in Europe, which is where you have anywhere from 10 to 12 weeks. And in some states, it's going to be less than that.",
